### Interpretation and follow-up questions

- Inspect repeated hits before interpreting the all-hit count as a count of distinct domains.
- How many accessory candidates recur on proteins with different PETadex HMM matches?
- How sensitive is the accessory set to the strict one-residue overlap rule and alignment versus envelope boundaries?
- Are unannotated stretches explained by incomplete scan coverage, regions outside known signatures, or possible new domains?
- After reviewing this test, set `TEST_PROTEINS=None` to measure coverage across the full input set.

Record biological conclusions after inspecting the generated tables and figures. No disorder filtering is part of this analysis.

