## Data archive — exact upload commands and access dates

These commands upload the inputs, this run's outputs and figures, scripts/provenance, notebook and requirements.
They are displayed even when `UPLOAD_ARCHIVE=False`. Set that flag to `True` and rerun this cell to perform the transfers.
Uploads require configured write access to `s3://petadex/`; no credentials are embedded here.

The access log records timestamps only when commands actually execute. Running the saved shell script directly does not
produce this Python access log; use this cell for the documented workflow.

upload_commands=[aws_cp(p,S3_PREFIX+'inputs/'+p.name) for p in (FASTA_FILE,INTERPRO_TSV,HMM_DOMTBLOUT)]
upload_commands += [
    aws_cp(run_path,S3_PREFIX+'runs/'+run_path.name+'/',recursive=True),
    aws_cp(run_figures,S3_PREFIX+'figures/'+run_path.name+'/',recursive=True),
